      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Which digits, when inserted into the blank, make the number $◻46\\,283\\,123$ divisible by $3?$\n\nI. $3$\n\nII. $6$\n\nIII. $9$",
      "worked_solution": "A number is divisible by $3$ if the sum of its digits is divisible by $3.$\n\nFor the number $◻46\\,283\\,123$ the sum of the digits is\n\n$$\n◻+4+6+2+8+3+1+2+3=29+◻.\n$$\n\nNow, let's consider each of the given digits that could be inserted into the blank.\n\n- If we insert $3$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+3=32,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- If we insert $6$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+6=35,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\n- If we insert $9$ into the blank, then the sum of the digits is $29+9=38,$ which is *not* divisible by $3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None.\"",
